<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-1335] Y Axis numbers truncated for large numbers on Area Graphs</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1335</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When large numbers are used on the Area Chart, the numbers flow off the side of the chart and appear truncated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://i.imgur.com/Nsgl61P.png&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://i.imgur.com/Nsgl61P.png&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To reproduce, enter the following Paragraph:&lt;br/&gt;
%sql SELECT 100000,100000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Run the paragraph, then click the Area Chart button.  Note that the Y-axis number is not fully shown.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
